[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. It is not one issue. The
reports merged into it describe three different problems, and the queued parser fix closes only
the first. Each problem now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
When the parser fix ships, keep #4471's reports from the <code>hint</code> and <code>day-shift</code>
rows open. Those people will still get the wrong day.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  repo="JanRubel/s01e03-what-it-shows"
  issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'day-shift': 3 }}
/>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so their dates come out with day and month swapped: "Our 7 April reminder went out on
4 July." This is the bug #4471 describes, and the fix queued for it.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`. People type what the hint says, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first.
The swap looks the same as `parser`, but the parser fix does not touch it: it only happens on the
form channel, only for tenants on booking-v3 (Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour). The fix
is the hint, or reading the date the way the hint asks for it.

**`day-shift`: the date moves by one day.** Nothing is swapped. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May.
Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." One
invite "arrived before I made the booking". That is a timezone or day-boundary bug, on any tenant
and any channel. The desk had already noted these reports as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`)
and filed them under `parser` anyway, because their tenant writes the day first.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

- Triage merges on the subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  The three problems share the same subjects ("Month and day swapped?", "Wrong day on the
  invite"), so subject matching cannot tell them apart. Both the triage page and decision 0001
  are past the 180-day review mark.
- Intake tags each report from the reporter's browser. That is a guess: the cause depends on the
  tenant's locale, booking form and channel ([how the desk tells causes apart](/kb/triage/dedupe)).
- The export repeats some reports across its pages. They are counted once here.

## What to do

1. Keep #4471 for `parser`. Its fix is queued.
2. Work `hint` and `day-shift` in their own tickets, with their own owners.
3. When a report says "one day off", read the body before merging: a flipped date and a moved
   date are different bugs.

